Exception covers libgcc, so images compiled with this bundle are unencumbered.
avr-libc is BSD-3-Clause.

The full Arduino core is NOT vendored. A minimal ATTinyCore subset (LGPL-2.1)
IS, in arduino-core/, for the `language: "arduino"` route on the ATtiny85 and
ATtiny88 only -- it is compiled server-side and never shipped to a client. The
posture is argued in NOTICE.md; this line used to say no core was vendored at
all, which stopped being true when that route landed.
